le payment options to patients; and digital intake and clinical data capture, patient engagement and activation tools, and measurement and analytics solutions. It also offers PhreesiaPads, a self-service intake tablets; and Arrivals Kiosks, which are on-site kiosks. The company serves a range of healthcare organizations including ambulatory practices, health systems, and hospitals, as well as life sciences companies, government entities, patient advocacy, public interest and not-for-profit and other organizations. Phreesia, Inc. was incorporated in 2005 and is based in Wilmington, Delaware.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Chaim  Indig | Co-Founder, CEO & Director | Age 46 | Compensation: $515,000 (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $269K ranks in the below the sector median among Healthcare peers, improving at 25%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $38K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $38K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Phreesia, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $783M market cap on $481M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +20% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -96% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $68M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 14 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 34.18\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","Accruals are elevated at -11.5% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin -1.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 14% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 6.4% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.6) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Priced near or above estimated fair value, so the margin of safety has been bid away","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.0825568694619453},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.1% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 52/100): durably derated by the market; leveraged balance sheet under pressure \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Insiders are net buyers (100% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 15% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.3% return)","Healthcare tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"(PHR) and the Role of Price-Sensitive Allocations","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/15/PHR_and_the_Role_of_Price-Sensitive_Allocations_110326013602_1793687762.html","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793687762.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Phreesia Sets Release Date for Fiscal Third Quarter 2027 Results","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/healthcare/articles/phreesia-sets-release-date-fiscal-211100832.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793913060.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Phreesia Director Lainie Goldstein Acquires 502 Deferred Stock Units in Quarterly Retainer Election","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/phreesia-director-lainie-goldstein-acquires-502-deferred-stock-units-in-quarterly-retainer-election","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793656476.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","m_and_a"]},{"title":"Phreesia's David Linetsky Amends RSU Tax Withholding Disclosure to Correct Filing Errors","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/phreesias-david-linetsky-amends-rsu-tax-withholding-disclosure-to-correct-filing-errors","date":"2026-10-28","timestamp":1793150675.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.34,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"BlackRock Portfolio Management Reports 5.1% Stake in P